WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.925
Last, what the assessor reads.

2
00:00:01.925 --> 00:00:06.862
The program's evidence is the records
the services keep, exported on a schedule

3
00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:11.875
and retained, for the configuration
management and flaw remediation controls.

4
00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:19.167
The control wording is from NIST SP
800-53 Revision 5, release 5.2.0,

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:25.187
which FedRAMP's 2026 catalog uses without
adding parameter values to these controls.

6
00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:30.354
CM-2, baseline configuration: the
policy library exported from Graph,

7
00:00:30.354 --> 00:00:33.888
under version control,
with its review history.

8
00:00:33.888 --> 00:00:37.397
CM-6, configuration
settings: per-setting status,

9
00:00:37.397 --> 00:00:43.188
the exception register with approvals,
and the Intune audit log of every change.

10
00:00:43.188 --> 00:00:47.832
CM-7, least functionality: attack
surface reduction in block,

11
00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:51.825
the firewall rule set, the
Edge extension allow list.

12
00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:56.112
CM-8, inventory: the
weekly reconciliation.

13
00:00:56.112 --> 00:01:01.587
SI-2, flaw remediation: the ring
table and per-ring compliance.

14
00:01:01.587 --> 00:01:05.004
SI-2's defined period is the
organization's parameter,

15
00:01:05.004 --> 00:01:07.412
and the ring deadlines are what set it.

16
00:01:07.412 --> 00:01:11.487
Two GCC facts change where
data and endpoints live.

17
00:01:11.487 --> 00:01:17.226
Intune in a GCC tenant isn't a separate
government instance: GCC uses the

18
00:01:17.226 --> 00:01:23.549
commercial service and worldwide Graph,
and only GCC High and DoD are separate.

19
00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:28.590
Defender for Endpoint for US Government
is built in Azure US Government,

20
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.286
with the GCC portal at security
dot microsoft dot com.

21
00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:37.914
And Windows Update for Business reports
don't meet GCC compliance requirements,

22
00:01:37.914 --> 00:01:41.862
so SI-2 evidence comes from
Intune and Autopatch reports.

23
00:01:41.862 --> 00:01:47.329
The program also maps this evidence to
FedRAMP 20x Key Security Indicators,

24
00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:52.225
as its own claim, written for cloud
service offerings, not an agency fleet.

25
00:01:52.225 --> 00:01:57.805
So, from Monday: inventory and triage every
GPO; set the tenant compliance defaults;

26
00:01:57.805 --> 00:02:01.908
carry procurement into the group
tag; onboard servers with a

27
00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:06.750
short-lived certificate principal;
and reconcile inventories weekly.

28
00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:11.025
Chapters 04 to 10 and
Appendix A carry the detail.

29
00:02:11.025 --> 00:02:11.860
Thank you.
